Approach:

On running system.out it generated questions like 
"Please set a password for your account:"
"How many bytes in length is your password?"
"Your successfully stored password:"
"Enter your hash to access your account!"

To find how hash is calculated i opened the binary in ghidra to take a look at the decompiled code.
The return value of make_secret() function is compared with the user input to print the flag.
This means this parameter has no effect on the return value.We also see that it is XORing each element in a global array 
obf_bytes[] with 0xaa. We follow the reference to obf_bytes[] and write the bytes down.And we continue inside the hash().
We then get the hash as -3209081493549540382

